{
  "name": "chip8",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "title": "CHIP-8 (Octax parity family)",
  "kind": "family",
  "note": "One CPU, 22 games. tools/bundle_chip8.mjs bundles ../../common/threefry2x32.js + src/*.js with one games/<game>.json and its ROM (base64) into dist/chip8_<game>.js plus a dist/chip8_<game>.json sidecar (per-game action space: the game's keypad keys in Octax's action_set order, then NOOP); tools/bundle_all.mjs does every game. Edit src/ and games/; never roms/ or dist/. The manifest deliberately has no `sources` key: tools/bundle_multifile.py --all would treat the family as one game.",
  "action_space": "per game: action_set keys in Octax index order, then NOOP last (sidecar)",
  "max_steps": 4500,
  "obs": {
    "rgb": true,
    "rgb_size": 64,
    "octax_frame_stack": 4,
    "note": "PlayTrain observes the display after each step (the last of Octax's 4 frames). Decided 2026-09-19 (PLAN section 9 Q1): last frame stays the default; a 'same observation as Octax' setup uses the runtime's frame_stack=4 in grayscale, which stacks the last four steps' displays (Octax stacks the four 11-instruction frames within one step, so the two stacks differ in time resolution)."
  },
  "human": {
    "steps_per_second": 15,
    "controls": "CHIP-8 keypad 1 2 3 C / 4 5 6 D / 7 8 9 E / A 0 B F on keys 1 2 3 4 / Q W E R / A S D F / Z X C V; each game names its keys in its sidecar.",
    "keymap_overlay": true
  },
  "reference": {
    "name": "Octax (Radji 2025, arXiv 2510.01764): JAX CHIP-8 emulator + 22 arcade games with register-read rewards",
    "repo": "https://github.com/riiswa/octax",
    "branch": "main",
    "commit": "3aa53b516152e97f2ed91eae6e33b6ee9a97596b",
    "cloned": "2026-09-19",
    "license": "MIT (code); ROMs per-game authorship in each module metadata, four are Octax-modified builds with .8o sources",
    "engine": [
      "octax/emulator.py",
      "octax/instructions/*.py",
      "octax/state.py",
      "octax/stack.py",
      "octax/decode.py"
    ],
    "env": "octax/env.py OctaxEnv, constructed as octax/environments/__init__.py create_environment does (disable_delay defaults False there)",
    "oracle_python": "3.12.9",
    "oracle_jax": "0.6.2",
    "oracle_flax": "0.10.7",
    "oracle_numpy": "2.2.6",
    "oracle_jax_threefry_partitionable": true,
    "step_semantics": "press action_set[a] (a == len(action_set) is NOOP); run (700 // 60) * 4 = 44 instructions; timers: zeroed if disable_delay else max(t - 1, 0) in uint8 (0 becomes 255); release the key; reward = score_fn(after) - score_fn(before); terminated = terminated_fn(after); truncated at time >= 4500. Startup instructions run once on PRNGKey(0); reset(rng) then replaces rng with PRNGKey(seed).",
    "parity": "full state every step: pc, I, V[0..15], stack pointer, stack[0..15], delay, sound, keypad[0..15], display sha1 (64x32 bools, x-major, packbits), rng key data, score, reward, terminated, truncated; same ROM bytes, seed and action sequence; tests/gate_oracle.mjs vs tests/oracle.py",
    "not_matched": [
      "pixels: Octax renders the 64x32 display at 8x (512x256 RGB); PlayTrain draws it 1:1 into the middle band of a 64x64 observation (rows 16..47) and shows a 256x256 canvas to humans, colours from the `classic` scheme only",
      "observation: Octax stacks the display after instruction 11, 22, 33 and 44 of each step (4 frames); PlayTrain observes the display after the step (the 4th of those frames). Human decision 2026-09-19: the last frame stays the default (obs.octax_frame_stack records Octax's count). frame_stack=4 grayscale in the runtime gives a 4-deep stack of consecutive STEP displays, not Octax's intra-step frames; the two are equal only when the display does not change within a step.",
      "the host reset consumes one NOOP frame before the first agent action (PlayTrain draws and steps in the same frame)",
      "termination: PlayTrain stops the episode at gameState GAMEOVER; Octax keeps stepping the terminated state (the lockstep gate compares those steps too)",
      "truncation at 4500 steps is the sidecar's max_steps, enforced by the runtime, not by the game",
      "sound: the sound timer is emulated bit-exactly, nothing is played",
      "two keys held by a human resolve to the lower action index; Octax's action space has one key per action, so the case never arises for an agent"
    ]
  },
