  "reference_quirks": [
    "octax/environments/__init__.py:64 create_environment defaults disable_delay to False; only brix, pong, shooting_stars, spacejam, tank, vertical_brix set True. OctaxEnv.__init__ default True is not what the games run with.",
    "octax/env.py step, disable_delay False: jnp.maximum(timer - 1, 0) on uint8; a timer at 0 becomes 255 every step (checked live: 0 -> 255, 1 -> 0).",
    "octax/instructions/alu.py execute_alu_operation: every 8XYN writes VF, including 8XY0-8XY3 (VF := 0) and undefined N (VX unchanged, VF := 0); when X == F the flag overwrites the result (8F14 with VF=200, V1=100 leaves VF = 1).",
    "octax/instructions/misc.py execute_font_character: FONT_START + VX * 5 is uint8 arithmetic; VX = 60 gives I = 124, not 380.",
    "octax/instructions/control_flow.py execute_jump_with_offset_modern: BXNN jumps to (NN + VX) & 0xFFF, i.e. into the font/zero page, never NNN + V0.",
    "octax/stack.py: no bounds check. 17 pushes leave pointer 17 with the 17th address dropped (scatter out of range is a no-op); a pop at pointer 0 yields pointer -1 and stack[15] (negative index wraps), and zeroes stack[15].",
    "octax/emulator.py fetch: memory[pc] / memory[pc+1] clamp out-of-range indices (pc 4095 reads memory[4095] twice); pc is uint16 and is not masked, so it can leave 0xFFF.",
    "octax/instructions/display.py: DXYN wraps the start coordinate and clips the sprite; VF = any(display & sprite) as a bool cast to uint8. execute_clear_screen uses jnp.empty_like, which is zeros in JAX.",
    "ROM sha1 in module metadata does not match the shipped file for: flight_runner, spacejam, worm. The levelled games (cavern, space_flight, target_shooter) carry metadata for other files entirely. The reference is the bytes in the pinned commit; roms.<file>.sha1 above is what the gate verifies.",
    "cavern4a.ch8 and cavern4b.ch8 cannot be loaded through create_environment (env_id must end in digits); the Octax paper's \"cavern 1-6\" reaches cavern1,2,3,5,6 only. Human decision 2026-09-19: both are shipped anyway; tests/oracle.py --module cavern builds OctaxEnv from the cavern module with the given ROM, and games/cavern4a.json / cavern4b.json carry oracle_module.",
    "Under uniform random actions (gate seeds 1-3, 500 steps) cavern2, cavern3, cavern5 and cavern6 terminate at step 2-3 and cavern1 at step 22-46 (V14 == 0); deep terminates at step 49 for every seed; airplane, blinky, rocket, shooting_stars, target_shooter1-3 and tetris never terminate within 500 steps. All of it matches Octax step for step; it is the ROMs' behaviour under Octax's timer rule, not a port bug.",
    "shooting_stars score_fn is `lax.cond(V0 > 128, uint8(0), V0)` (0 once V0 exceeds 128); airplane's `-V11 - V12` is uint8 arithmetic (wraps); both are transcribed as typed expression trees in games/*.json and checked by the lockstep gate."
  ]
